.TH SDL_HINT_ANDROID_AAUDIO_INPUT_PRESET 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_ANDROID_AAUDIO_INPUT_PRESET \- A variable to control Android\(aqs AAudio input preset.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_ANDROID_AAUDIO_INPUT_PRESET \(dqSDL_ANDROID_AAUDIO_INPUT_PRESET\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This hint only applies to SDL\(aqs \(dqaaudio\(dq backend on Android 9+ devices\[char46]
.PP
Some devices choose the wrong microphone by default (between the one meant to be spoken in when the phone is held to the user\(aqs ear for a phone call, or an external microphone that\(aqs meant to be used when recording video), or have DSP effects applied to the recorded audio, and changing the input preset can help control this\[char46]
.PP
This can be any number that maps to an
.BR AAUDIO_INPUT_PRESET_*
enum from the Android NDK headers\[char46] The most reasonable choices are 5 (\(dqcamcorder\(dq, for external microphones) and 7 (\(dqvoice communication\(dq, for speaking directly into the device like a mobile phone)\[char46] 6 (\(dqvoice recognition\(dq) might also be a useful choice\[char46]
.PP
If unset (the default), SDL will not specify an input preset at all, which lets the system choose\[char46] This is usually the correct thing to do unless your app is having problems\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before a recording audio device is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]16\[char46]

